some four million people have left  ukraine as the war with russia continues  many looking for sanctuary the response  has been swift by the west it makes  alfred melwatch proud to see the lengths  the canadian government is going to to  help people in need but it has also left  him with questions that is how they  should be responding um but we also got  to notice that  there's a lot of  ukrainian connection within the  government they're going to have a  better voice at the highest level than  other refugees for sure alfred fled  south sudan after civil war broke out  when he was nine years old he lived in a  kenyan refugee camp for more than a  decade before coming to canada in 2011  on a university scholarship  seeing the speed and options western  nations have made available for  ukrainians has been evident to some ngos  one human rights researcher says  european countries like poland have been  championed for their ability to bring in  the amount of people fleeing violence  but at the same time they have  introduced measures of blocking others  from entering the country helena cesar  with amnesty international says several  thousand syrian migrants are trapped on  the polish border with belarus after  that country looked to deport them and  poland refuses to grant the syrians  asylum on the border with ukraine  they're hailed as heroes they're  venerated  and on the other hand they are being  criminalized on this border  the syrian refugee crisis also pointed  to the willingness of western nations to  help the millions who were fleeing the  middle eastern country author serena  parekh says the ukrainian refugee model  is one that needs to be used in the  future so that  every refugee child can be greeted with  a stuffed animal and a chocolate bar  and not just the ones who are  quote-unquote like us  the visas ottawa made available for  ukrainians with canadian family are  flexible something that has never been  done before in a statement to global  news the immigration minister says the  country continues to resettle refugees  from around the world including the  middle east and north africa sean fraser  says quote we remain committed to the  refugee resettlement program and we will  continue to welcome refugees to canada  as conditions allow kyle benning global  news
 

